Tournament Analysis
  vertices: speed-set time words
  observable: density, stabilizer size, Fourier entropy/top mode, period
  switch: harder = lower density, more folding, lower entropy, stronger mode
  fingerprints: {'vertices': ['AP_wall', 'V_star_wall', 'near_AP_apex', 'S562_packet_n14', 'S562_packet_n14_lift', 'no_small_pinch_proxy', 'random_low_resonance'], 'score_hist': {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}, 'directed_3_cycles': 0, 'sccs': [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1], 'hamiltonian_paths': 1}

Synthesis
  Raw primitive reset time is one lap, so it does not classify integer rows.
  The useful reset invariant is the finite time word: period, stabilizer,
  and Fourier character support.  Burnside becomes legal after replacing
  the full shift group by the stabilizer K of that word.
  Pair-sum and n-clock witnesses are visible as time-word frequencies;
  the next proof object should combine S570 witness-or-core with this
  Fourier/stabilizer ledger on owner-labelled time events.
